WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.400
Speaker 1: Today we have two stories about Russian&nbsp;
prisons, quite frankly. A number of you wrote to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:13.840
me yesterday and you sent me an article about a&nbsp;
teacher being imprisoned for political speech in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:19.040
Russia and said, David, is this the woman who&nbsp;
called in to your show a few months ago? Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.320
I've already looked. I don't believe it is the&nbsp;
same woman unless the woman who called in was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.160
deliberately giving wrong information about&nbsp;
where she teaches and different things. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:35.760
it is a very cautionary tale about what exactly&nbsp;
was said by our caller and what she feared because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:41.920
of her political views. So let me reset it for&nbsp;
you. Article says Russian Teacher Sentenced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:48.640
For Telling Students About War Crimes in&nbsp;
Ukraine. This article is about Irina again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:55.840
who received a five year suspended sentence and&nbsp;
has been barred from working in state schools. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.600
if you read the article, it says this is a school&nbsp;
teacher in a provincial, provincial Russian city.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.440
She got a suspended sentence because she spoke&nbsp;
out against the Kremlin's invasion of Ukraine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.760
and she was found guilty of discrediting the&nbsp;
Russian armed forces. There is a new law that bans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:19.280
criticism of the war in Ukraine and she got a five&nbsp;
year suspended sentence and is barred from working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:26.800
in state schools for three years. The court also&nbsp;
found that she disseminated false information by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:33.680
telling students about the siege of Mariupol and&nbsp;
Russian airstrikes killing children in Ukraine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:39.840
She was slapped with charges in March. So this was&nbsp;
actually this predates our caller. But remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:48.720
the caller we had who called in under a pseudonym&nbsp;
for exactly these types of fears. Listen to this.&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.960
Speaker 2: Taking my question.
Speaker 1: So before you go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:54.560
you're calling from Russia?
Speaker 2: Yeah, from Moscow.&nbsp;

00:01:54.560 --> 00:02:00.240
Speaker 1: And so what is the would you say&nbsp;
the general sentiment there is that people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.080
like the invasion of Ukraine or people&nbsp;
are against the invasion of Ukraine?&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.680
Speaker 2: I have to say that I will have a&nbsp;
certain Moscow liberal bias because that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:15.760
the area where I was raised and my family has&nbsp;
always been critical of the government. There is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:23.120
not a single person in my immediate circles that&nbsp;
are fans of this government. Okay. But I will say&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.480
that's just from my own personal experience,&nbsp;
just looking at cars or driving or parking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:35.600
anywhere. I don't see a single Z sign. There&nbsp;
is no single, I would say, personal initiative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:43.120
to install anything that is commemorative to this&nbsp;
war. All I've seen is state council local efforts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:47.760
which are sponsored from the state, from the&nbsp;
federal budget to try and convince people to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:53.760
engage in such practices and some type of coercion&nbsp;
that's happening, for example, in kindergartens.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:58.640
Oftentimes, parents discover that the school trip&nbsp;
or the kindergarten trip they send their children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:06.480
to was actually a sort of patriotic event because&nbsp;
they then later find pictures of the children&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.440
posed in the letter Z on social media.
Speaker 1: That's the patriotic education&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:15.120
Trump keeps talking about. Now, listen,&nbsp;
do you feel safe expressing your views,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:21.040
antagonistic to the government?
Speaker 2: On here he has over at my university.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.520
I've already sort of spoken myself into&nbsp;
15 years of prison, if anybody would like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:35.600
deep, deep anywhere around me. So this is just a&nbsp;
weird spaces that I know that if anybody looked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:41.360
at me or what I've been writing, what I've been&nbsp;
saying, it is quite possible that I will face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:46.400
some sort of fine or maybe even jail time.&nbsp;
After all, our person was arrested yesterday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:51.741
for walking out with a printout of Russian&nbsp;
constitution on the streets and couldn't walk.&nbsp;

00:03:51.741 --> 00:03:59.040
Speaker 1: So obviously not the same person. Our&nbsp;
caller called in May and we know that Iran again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:04.880
